{{!
    @template mod_redaction/grading_shell

    Layout of the grading page of the classic mode: navigation, the submission on the left, AI evaluation and grade on the right.
    The parts are rendered by their own templates and given as HTML.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * navigation - HTML of the navigation bar
    * hassubmissions - Whether there is a submission to show
    * timeline - HTML of the training timeline, may be empty
    * submissionpanel - HTML of the submission
    * aievaluation - HTML of the AI evaluations, may be empty
    * gradingform - HTML of the grading form

    Example context (json):
    {
        "navigation": "<div>Navigation</div>",
        "hassubmissions": true,
        "timeline": "",
        "submissionpanel": "<div>Copie</div>",
        "aievaluation": "",
        "gradingform": "<form></form>"
    }
}}
<div class="mod_redaction-grading-container">
    {{{navigation}}}
    {{#hassubmissions}}
        <div class="mod_redaction-submission-panel">
            {{{timeline}}}
            {{{submissionpanel}}}
            <div class="mod_redaction-grading-sidebar">
                {{{aievaluation}}}
                {{{gradingform}}}
            </div>
        </div>
    {{/hassubmissions}}
    {{^hassubmissions}}
        <div class="alert alert-warning">{{#str}}no_submission, mod_redaction{{/str}}</div>
    {{/hassubmissions}}
</div>
